  "slug": "discovery-database-1f96",
  "summary": "New update papers from CIViC, canSAR, HIPPIE, DGIdb and others pair coverage growth with ML-assisted curation, prediction and interoperable access.",
  "synthesis": "Annual updates to established curated resources dominate. They expand coverage while adding machine-facing access and AI-assisted curation or prediction. HIPPIE 3.0 reaches about 1.2M experimentally supported human PPIs. FusionGDB 3.0 holds 156K fusion genes from RNA-seq and WGS breakpoints, PRGdb 5.0 grows to 874,967 candidate plant resistance proteins, and VEuPathDB lists 2,602 datasets. AI enters at two points. For curation, there is AI-guided curation in CIViC, AI-assisted curation in VEuPathDB, and new ML annotations in Europe PMC. For prediction, canSAR adds ML predictors and agentic-AI protein tools, PRGdb adds DREM deep-learning prioritization, and HIPPIE adds negative training sets for interaction prediction. Interoperability is a third axis. DGIdb adds Python/R clients, Docker images and versioned releases, CIViC submits to ClinVar, and the IGVF Data Portal preprint offers an API, knowledge-graph-integrated results and agentic tooling. Expert curation also continues in CDD and in CiliaHub, which covers over 2,500 ciliary genes with ClinVar variants, while CNCB-NGDC adds thirteen new resources.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
